Z||000000||theogre||05-19-2000||09:24 AM||||Please note, there is a new variant of the love bug running around. This one is slower but does real damage.<P>It's subject line is FW:XXXXXXXXXXX where X can be the subject of any old mail on the infected machine that sent it. It likely won't be the same twice. The message section contains only a VBscript attachment, no text, acording to published reports.<P>Microsoft has posted a critical update they claim helps prevent this type thing from operating so easily. You can get it at:<P><A HREF="http://windowsupdate.microsoft.com" TARGET=_blank>windowsupdate.microsoft.com</A> This works for all win9x and winNT machines. Yes the WinNT service pack is available thru this link as is the 128bit encryption update for all versions of I.E.<P>or by clicking windows update on the start button menu on win98 machines.<P>To check encryption stregnth click help/about in internet exploder. If it says 40 bits get the update to 128. DO NOT use 40 bit encryption for credit card transactions on secure web sites. (U.S. export restictions on encryption have recently changed. Most everyone can use 128 now except some embargoed countries. read the Microsoft site for more information.)||||reg||4
Z||000001||FieroGTGirl||05-19-2000||10:40 AM||||Thanks for the valueable info!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-19-2000||10:53 AM||||Correction:<P>The microsoft update for this type virus is not yet available. It will be at the links above when it is.<P>For now there are other updates there and you want all those as well.<P>There is also a "service pack" for original win98. It's in the "recomended updates" section further down the list. install that as well.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-19-2000||02:35 PM||||Ogre--I have MS Outlook.  I kinda like it for the features (I'm not very computer-ish.).  Do I have to open the attachment to let the beast loose or will it invade my happy home just by opening the email?  How can I delete an email without becoming FUBAR??  I really don't want to change email programs.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||05-21-2000||12:09 PM||||Monkeyman, You gotta open the attachment to unleash this one. You might want to look around in your Outlook program and turn off auto-preview or the "preview message" pane.<BR>You didn't mention what version of Outlook you are using, but if it has the option of using MS Word as the e-mail editor, turn it off. <BR>BTW... At work, we didn't see *even one* instance of this latest virus. Possibly because the "filtering" on our mail system is actually working.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||05-21-2000||03:57 PM||||Is there a way to disable scripting in Outlook 2000? I get a daily email newsletter from lockergnome.com (highly recommended) and I would like to keep receiving that. However, I'd like to disable all other html emails, scripting, etc..||||reg||5
